Leave the PuTTY section when random_add_noise returns early.

random_add_noise enters putty_section and returns without leaving it when
the generator is not active. The section is recursive, so the returning
thread carries on, but every other thread then blocks for good on its next
entry -- another session's sockets, RNG or bignums. The early return now
leaves the section first. Line counts are unchanged.

Reported upstream with the same fix: https://github.com/winscp/winscp/pull/74

--- a/source/putty/sshrand.c
+++ b/source/putty/sshrand.c
@@ -41,2 +41,2 @@
     if (!random_active)
-        return;
+        { WINSCP_PUTTY_SECTION_LEAVE; return; } // linscp: do not return holding the section
